    'Run an ordered sequence of actions against d1 and d2.\n' +
    '\n' +
    'How to use this operation\n' +
    '\n' +
    "Act accepts steps through --input. Activate the tab and take a fresh snapshot first; inactive interaction fails before dispatch. A failed sequence reports completed steps and whether the failing step was dispatched. Element actions use d1:/d2: references from snapshot; --human true uses an eased visible cursor path. Upload targets a file input reference and accepts local file paths; absolute paths use the desktop filesystem and relative paths use the App's storage directory.\n" +
    '\n' +
    'Examples\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  Click and wait\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  {\n' +
    `    "command": "penkra tabs act --input '{\\"tabId\\":\\"<tab-id>\\",\\"steps\\":[{\\"action\\":\\"click\\",\\"ref\\":\\"d1:e3\\"},{\\"action\\":\\"wait\\",\\"document\\":\\"d1\\",\\"text\\":\\"Saved\\"}]}'"\n` +
    '  }\n' +
    '\n' +
    'Input fields\n' +
    '  --steps <array>  required.\n' +
    '  --tab-id <string>  required. Exact retained App tab ID returned by penkra tabs list.\n' +
    '  --human <boolean>  optional.\n' +
    '\n' +
    'Invocation\n' +
    '  Send one ordinary command string. Pass each input field by name exactly as listed\n' +
    '  under Input fields (for example --thread-id <id>). A bare value without its --name\n' +
